vine 1.2.0
prefix: caravan
title: Caravan of Seasons build graph
---
[root] Caravan anchor implementation (packet plan) (planning)
Execute the independent packets below. Keep SDK objects separate from Caravan game objects, use direct indexed queries rather than interval stepping, and dispatch packets only after their dependencies are reviewed. The cellular automata anchor proposal is the shared behavior target. Files: proposals/cellular-automata-anchor.md; proposals/semantic-contract.md; roadmap.md; spec/initial.md
-> anchor-demo
-> benchmarks
-> branch-model
-> contract-gate
-> domain-model
-> hazard-rules
-> indexed-query
-> journal-writer
-> lookahead
-> persistence
-> presentation
-> productization
-> proof-package
-> purity-hardening
-> reference-oracle
-> sdk-envelopes
-> seeded-journal
-> vegetation-rules
-> workspace-time
@guidance text/markdown spec/initial.md
---
[contract-gate] Anchor contract gate (reviewing)
Files: proposals/semantic-contract.md; proposals/cellular-automata-anchor.md; spec/initial.md
Do: Freeze the anchor decisions that are already settled: one-second game ticks, arbitrary continuous t_ sampling, empty journal as empty set, journal-owned saucer creation, postdated entries, three layers, direct indexed queries, and SDK/game-object separation. Record only the remaining implementation-level choices.
Accept: The implementation packets can consume one coherent contract without importing the removed interval-fold model.
---
[workspace-time] Workspace and time module (notstarted)
Files: Cargo.toml; crates/engine-time/**
Do: Bootstrap the Rust workspace and implement distinct LogicalTime and Tau wrappers with the approved signed i64 representation, one-second anchor game-tick relation, checked arithmetic, ordering, and exact equality. Keep raw time arithmetic in this crate.
Accept: Boundary and overflow tests pass; no game-domain types or evaluator logic are owned here.
-> contract-gate
---
[sdk-envelopes] SDK envelopes and query contracts (notstarted)
Files: crates/engine-sdk/**
Do: Define generic SDK objects and traits for Context, JournalEntry, Journal, Worldline, GameState, Playback, Frame, and typed query results without admitting interval callbacks or game-domain primitives. Keep game payloads opaque to the SDK.
Accept: SDK/game ownership is visible in types; immutable inputs and owned query outputs are expressible; no actor, terrain, saucer, or resource type is introduced.
-> contract-gate
-> workspace-time
---
[domain-model] Saucer geometry and game layers (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-domain/**
Do: Define axial radius-5 geometry, the 91-tile set, fixed neighbor order, terrain, actor, effect, resource, identifiers, and compact game journal entry payloads. Own game meaning only; do not implement journal storage or evaluation.
Accept: Geometry and layer tests establish 91 tiles, six neighbors, valid tile identities, and the three-layer representation.
-> contract-gate
-> workspace-time
---
[journal-writer] Journal writer and entries (notstarted)
Files: crates/engine-journal/**
Do: Implement immutable journal values and a journal-owned monotonic writer that can postdate entries before evaluation, preserve equal-time append order, and publish typed game entries without caller-owned timestamps.
Accept: Writer tests cover advance_to, record, postdated visibility, backward rejection, empty journals, and exact target-time inclusion. No branch correction logic is owned here.
-> domain-model
-> sdk-envelopes
---
[branch-model] Counterfactual and corrected branches (notstarted)
Files: crates/engine-branches/**
Do: Implement immutable inclusive-prefix branch construction for counterfactual and corrected suffixes. Preserve parent journals, retain fork boundaries, and expose one branch value to the query layer.
Accept: Tests prove prefix agreement, suffix replacement, late-entry correction, parent/child isolation, and nested branch behavior without merge or networking.
-> journal-writer
-> sdk-envelopes
---
[indexed-query] Direct indexed query kernel (notstarted)
Files: crates/engine-index/**
Do: Implement the generic direct query boundary: select the game-tick index from t_, expose journal entries visible at t_, and return a new GameState without prior-state input, stepping API, or evaluator-owned RNG.
Accept: Empty journal, saucer creation, postdated entries, arbitrary query order, within-tick stability under a fixed journal, and journal-time discontinuities are testable.
-> domain-model
-> journal-writer
-> sdk-envelopes
---
[vegetation-rules] Vegetation rule definitions (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-vegetation/**
Do: Implement pure indexed definitions for Farmer, Wheat, Forest, and Forester, including fixed neighbor selection, destination wheat placement, wheat totals, and wood production. Return values; do not mutate snapshots.
Accept: Isolated rule traces cover each definition and use stable identifiers/order only.
-> domain-model
-> indexed-query
---
[hazard-rules] Hazard and conflict definitions (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-hazards/**
Do: Implement pure indexed definitions for Arsonist, Fire, Fighter, and Arborist, including target selection, fire ages/spread/destruction, collision, and three-tick conversion.
Accept: Isolated deterministic traces cover each rule, layer interactions, and conflict outcomes without actor execution order.
-> domain-model
-> indexed-query
---
[seeded-journal] Deterministic seeded journal fixture (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-seeded/**
Do: Generate the finite postdated spawn schedule from a fixed seed before evaluation: three actors every ten game ticks, valid unoccupied tiles, deterministic retries, and a hand-authored behavior trace alongside the generated trace.
Accept: Same seed yields identical ordered journal entries on every supported run; evaluator never owns the RNG.
-> domain-model
-> journal-writer
---
[reference-oracle] Anchor state oracle (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-reference/**
Do: Compose the game-domain definitions into the reference state(worldline, t_) oracle over terrain, actors, effects, and resources. Keep all derived results as query outputs.
Accept: The full anchor behavior is reproducible at arbitrary t_, in non-monotonic query order, over actual/counterfactual/corrected branches, with exact GameState logical time.
-> branch-model
-> hazard-rules
-> indexed-query
-> seeded-journal
-> vegetation-rules
---
[lookahead] Indexed lookahead and branch views (notstarted)
Files: crates/engine-lookahead/**
Do: Expose future queries and branch selection through the same direct oracle while keeping the journal fixed. No future entries are generated.
Accept: Earlier lookahead values remain unchanged when new values are authored on another branch; actual and alternate worlds use identical query machinery.
-> branch-model
-> reference-oracle
